**Data Engineering, Team Lead – Remote (US)**  
**Reports to:** SVP, Data & Platform  
**Salary Range:** $150,000 – $180,000 + bonus  

**Overview:**  
Lead the modernization and scaling of Get Well’s cloud-native data platform while mentoring and growing a high-performing engineering team. This role combines technical architecture ownership with people leadership, enabling advanced analytics and AI in a healthcare context that impacts millions of patients annually.

**Key Responsibilities:**  
- Own and evolve the architecture for ingestion, transformation, storage, and data access (lakehouse, data mesh, medallion).  
- Modernize legacy pipelines to AWS-native/serverless platforms (Glue, S3, Athena, Redshift, MSK, Lambda).  
- Design and operate both batch and streaming data pipelines across multiple data sources and formats.  
- Ensure platform readiness for analytics, AI/ML, and regulatory reporting.  
- Oversee deployment/orchestration with tools like Airflow, dbt, Spark, Databricks, Snowflake.  
- Partner on governance, quality, security, and compliance (HIPAA, HITRUST, FedRAMP).  
- Lead, mentor, and coach a distributed team of data engineers.  
- Drive best practices for CI/CD, observability, automation, and scalability.  

**Qualifications:**  
- 6+ years in data engineering/platform roles; 3+ years in technical leadership.  
- Proven experience building cloud-native data platforms in healthcare or similarly regulated domains.  
- Strong skills in Python, SQL, Spark, Kafka/MSK, dbt, Airflow, AWS data services.  
- Experience with streaming architectures and infrastructure-as-code (Terraform, CloudFormation, etc.).  
- Understanding of SMART on FHIR and healthcare compliance frameworks.  

**About Get Well:**  
A mission-driven healthcare technology company, part of SAI Group, serving 10M+ patients/year across 1,000+ sites. Recognized by KLAS and AVIA Marketplace for digital patient engagement solutions.

**Benefits:**  
Generous paid time off, multiple leave programs, 401(k) + incentives, comprehensive health benefits, professional development, wellness perks, and a supportive, flexible work environment.
